 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>A <b>cookie</b> is a small piece of text (name=value) stored in the browser by the server and sent back with every request. Used for remembering users.</p><h3>Steps / methods</h3><ul><li>Create: <code>Cookie c = new Cookie(\"user\", \"Samrat\");</code></li><li>Set life: <code>c.setMaxAge(seconds)</code> (0 deletes it).</li><li>Send: <code>res.addCookie(c);</code></li><li>Read: <code>Cookie[] cs = req.getCookies();</code> then <code>getName()</code>, <code>getValue()</code>.</li></ul><h3>Disadvantages</h3><ul><li>User can disable/delete cookies.</li><li>Only text, small size (~4 KB).</li><li>Not safe for secret data.</li></ul>",
 "quiz": {
